# -*- mode: Python -*-

# Multi-worktree e2e fixture — the incidents-admin shape in miniature
# (.agents/drafts/multi-worktree-parallel.md §11: local_resource + shared
# resources, no cluster).
#
# The SAME Tiltfile executes once per run (plan §3) with no branching:
# every resource declares its scope, and each run instantiates only what
# its scope names. Run with:
#
#   tilt up --worktrees
#
# Discovery is position-based (plan §2): every subdirectory of .worktree/
# containing a Tiltfile is a worktree named after its basename. The
# .worktree/wt-a and .worktree/wt-b checkouts here are strict pointers —
# each contains only `load_dynamic('../Tiltfile')` — so the run executes
# this root Tiltfile re-rooted at the checkout (plan §3 one-Tiltfile style;
# worktree.dir() == the checkout).

worktree_config(port_range=(10071, 10080))

# ── shared foundation (incidents-admin's postgres/admin-bff-image layer) ──
# Instantiated ONCE, in the main run only; worktree runs inherit it through
# dep resolution and never re-run it. scope="main" replaces the classic
# `if worktree.name() == ""` branch.
local_resource('shared-infra',
               cmd='true',
               serve_cmd='./serve.sh shared 10070',
               serve_port=10070,
               scope='main',
               links=['http://localhost:10070'])

# ── branch-local server ──
# One resource declaration for every worktree: instantiated once per
# worktree run, never in the main run, and engine-prefixed to
# wt:<worktree>_app at the boundary. serve_port is a request — the port
# registry deconflicts it per worktree: whichever run's Tiltfile loads
# first keeps 10071, the other gets the next free pool port. The
# allocated port is always injected as $TILT_SERVE_PORT (even when the
# request is honored — the authored value is only a request), and
# serve_cmd is a string so the shell expands it.
local_resource('app',
               cmd='true',
               serve_cmd='./serve.sh ' + worktree.name() + ' $TILT_SERVE_PORT',
               serve_port=10071,
               scope='worktree')
